  "question": {
    "text": "A student measured the diameter of a wire using a screw gauge with the least count $0.001 \\mathrm{~cm}$ and listed the measurements. The measured value should be recorded as",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ZgQOh",
      "text": "\n$5.3200 \\mathrm{~cm}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "67Pzg",
      "text": "\n$5.3 \\mathrm{~cm}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XHimK",
      "text": "\n$5.32 \\mathrm{~cm}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tsgC2",
      "text": "\n$5.320 \\mathrm{~cm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The least count (L.C.) of a screw guage is the smallest length which can be measured accurately with it.\nAs least count is $0.001 \\mathrm{~cm}=\\frac{1}{1000} \\mathrm{~cm}$\nHence measured value should be recorded upto 3 decimal places i.e., $5.320 \\mathrm{~cm}$",
    "image": null
  },
